   "say": [
    {
     "at": 1.0,
     "text": "This video sets the throws of a rudder with the R C bench. The bench drives the servo, measures the surface's angle with a sensor, and programs the servo's end points until both throws match."
    },
    {
     "at": 17.28,
     "text": "The example is a flap in a slice of wing. A K S T X 10 lies under the skin on a frame with a counter bearing, and moves the flap through a push rod."
    },
    {
     "at": 30.12,
     "text": "Step 1. Stick a pad of double sided gel tape onto the flap."
    },
    {
     "at": 35.84,
     "text": "Press the sensor onto the pad. Its X or Y axis has to run along the hinge line. The bench refuses the Z axis."
    },
    {
     "at": 45.56,
     "text": "Plug the servo into a programming port of the bench."
    }
   ]
  },
